e the nature of rain sound: Rain sounds like continuous, diffuse water impact or white noise.\n2.  Evaluate Option A (waterfall): Rushing water, similar to heavy rain. Mistakable.\n3.  Evaluate Option B (static noise): White noise, similar to moderate rain. Mistakable.\n4.  Evaluate Option C (car engine starting): Mechanical, intermittent, and distinct sounds (cranking, ignition). Not similar to rain. Not mistakable.\n5.  Evaluate Option D (shower running): Flowing water, very similar to rain. Mistakable.\n6.  The sound event that could *not* be mistaken for rain falling is the car engine starting.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{C}
