ling).\n\nIf we strictly follow the previous answer's structure (D: first speaker neutral, second speaker sadness):\nFirst Speaker: Neutral (Polite statements, flat final response).\nSecond Speaker: Sadness (Interpreting the sharp, exaggerated tone as masking negative emotion/disappointment).\n\nThis aligns best with the structure of Option D, even if the emotional labels are slightly ambiguous based purely on tone.\n\nFinal selection based on fitting the provided options to the auditory evidence, acknowledging the ambiguity: D.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
