r fluctuation and change in emotional expression (excitement $\rightarrow$ calm $\rightarrow$ surprise/confusion).\n    *   The second speaker remains consistently brief and neutral ("Fine").\n\n4.  **Conclusion:** The first speaker exhibits detectable changes in emotional tone and expression throughout the dialogue, whereas the second speaker does not.\n\n**Selection:** The emotional state of the first speaker changed.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
